==Battleground==
*2 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[THE FOLIVOREAN]] spawns as the boss after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Casaurian Darkjo]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*8 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*4 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 103.33 seconds<sup>3,100f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
You don't need to bring any [[Shield Piercing|Shield Piercers]] to this stage, as even at 200%, THE FOLIVOREAN's shield is still relatively weak. Instead, focus on bring counters to the Casaurian Darkjo, as once it is gone, the remaining threats will fall easily. Use [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] to burst down the starting Sir Seal, then stall THE FOLIVOREAN until Darkjo spawns. Bring [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] for Darkjo, and a high level [[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]] to tank Wild Doge's onslaught. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] is also recommended to slow the bosses down, especially with his [[Slow]] [[Talents|Talent]] maxed out.

Alternatively, you can defeat THE FOLIVOREAN quickly so that Darkjo won't be much of a problem. Burst down its Shield with [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]], then start spam [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cats]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cats]], along with adequate counters for Darkjo.

